    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26600" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĭgūrītor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĭgurr-</span></b> ),
			ōris, m.
		id.. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>One fond of dainties, an epicure, gourmand</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eumque quasi liguritorem catillonem appellat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			mal. part., <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 128</span></i>
			<i>in lemm</i>.</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> ‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĭgūrĭus</span></b> ,
				gulosus, catillo, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίχνος</span>, Gloss.</div>
